    "protein_name": "Lipoprotein LprI",
    "ec": [],
    "function": "Strongly binds and inhibits lysozyme, may help bacteria survive in lysozyme-producing host cells. When overexpressed in M.tuberculosis or M.smegmatis increases resistance to hen egg white lysozyme. M.smegmatis overexpressing LprI survive better during intracellular infection of peritoneal and monocyte-derived macrophages, both of which produce lysozyme during infection; M.smegmatis does not encode this protein. Somewhat better survival is seen in human cell lines when M.smegmatis cells express both proteins from this operon, i.e. GlbN (HbN) and LprI",
